          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab-enriched+category"} Ab-enriched category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
            factorization of a morphism by first forming its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
            and then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
            of the kernel. Similarly, in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+category"} regular category
            we can produce an image factorization by first forming the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel+pair"} kernel pair
            and then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizer"} coequalizer
            of the kernel pair. Several similar situations arise in the study of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-categories"} 2-categories
            as well. The theory of
            %strong generalized kernels
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+categories"} enriched categories
            subsumes all of these examples.
          %h2#generalized_kernels_and_their_quotients Generalized kernels and their quotients
          %p
            Let
